-- title:
--   Poles of j on X₁(M) counted by cusps
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be an algebraically closed field equipped with a $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra structure (so of characteristic $0$), and let $M$ be a nonzero natural number. Write $F$ for [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange K (ModularCurve.qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ (CongruenceSubgroup.Gamma1 M))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), that is: inside $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ one forms the subfield `qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ (Gamma1 M)` generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by all quotients $\mathrm{intSeriesC}\,\mathbb{Q}\,p_f/\mathrm{intSeriesC}\,\mathbb{Q}\,p_g$ attached to pairs of modular forms $f,g$ of some weight $k$ for $\Gamma_1(M)$ having integral $q$-expansions $p_f,p_g\in\mathbb{Z}[[q]]$ with the series of $p_g$ nonzero, and $F\subseteq K((q))$ is the subfield generated over $K$ by the image of that field under the coefficientwise map induced by $\mathbb{Q}\to K$. Let $y\in F$ be an element whose underlying Laurent series is [`ModularCurve.jqModC K`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L15), namely $q^{-1}$ times the image in $K[[q]]$ of the integral power series `jNum` $=E_4^3\cdot$ `dedekindEtaUnitInv`; thus $y$ is the modular invariant $j$, pinned by its $q$-expansion. The assertion is an equality of cardinalities: the number of places $P$ of $F$ over $K$ — valuation subrings of $F$ containing $K$, distinct from $F$, whose valuation ring is a principal ideal ring — with $P.\mathrm{ord}\,y<0$, the order being $-\log$ of the associated adic valuation, equals the number of double cosets $\Gamma_1(M)\backslash \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})/\langle T,-1\rangle$, where $\langle T,-1\rangle$ is the join of the cyclic subgroups generated by $T$ and by $-1$.
--
--   This is the statement that the poles of $j$ on the curve $X_1(M)$, taken over an algebraically closed base field of characteristic $0$, are in bijection with the cusps of $\pm\Gamma_1(M)$, the latter being described group-theoretically as double cosets of $\Gamma_1(M)$ against the stabiliser $\langle T,-1\rangle$ of the cusp $\infty$. It feeds the computation of the local contribution $-\operatorname{ord}_P j$ at a cusp in terms of its width, and the genus formula for $X_1(M)$ expressed as $12g+6\,\#\mathrm{cusps}=[\,\Gamma_1(M)\!\cdot\!\{\pm1\}:\text{index}\,]+12$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_natCard_place_ord_neg_laurentBaseChange_gamma1_eq_natCard_doubleCoset.lean

